# Binary files git must not "helpfully" convert line endings in.
#
# This machine checks out with CRLF, and without these rules git treats a PDF
# or a PNG as text: every 0x0A inside the file becomes 0x0D 0x0A on checkout and
# the file is corrupt. It committed fine, it just cannot be opened again.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.3mf   binary
*.stl   binary
*.glb   binary

# Generated files, compared against freshly generated text on every test run.
#
# web/build-guides.mjs writes LF and --check diffs what it would write against
# what is committed. This machine checks out with core.autocrlf=true, so
# without these rules a fresh clone gets CRLF on disk, every byte comparison
# fails, and tests/test_guides.py reports six pages as out of date when not one
# word has changed. Pinning them to LF makes the working copy the same on every
# machine, which is the only way a byte comparison means anything.
web/public/*.html   text eol=lf
web/public/robots.txt   text eol=lf
web/public/sitemap.xml  text eol=lf
